{
  "requirement": "Lists the selectable items from a single parse, including the root for the whole file.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Outline {\n    pub items: Vec<OutlineItem>,\n}\n\nimpl Outline {\n    pub fn new(items: Vec<OutlineItem>) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Outline;\nimpl Debug for Outline;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.outlines.Outline` is a declaration-only contract. It specifies a `#[non_exhaustive]` `pub struct Outline` with one public field, `items: Vec<OutlineItem>`. It specifies a constructor, `Outline::new(items: Vec<OutlineItem>) -> Self`. It also specifies the trait impls `Clone` and `Debug`. The `Lists the selectable items…` prose describes what the type is for. The accessor that produces the outline, `OutlineContent::outline`, is covered by the separate requirement `requirements.sdk.outlines.items`.\n\nThe requirement declares `:test: crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]`. That test runs `cargo doc` and walks the rustdoc HTML for every public export. It then calls `check_declaration` on each non-module item. `Outline` is in the inventory `md/requirements/sdk/public-api.md`, linked to the requirement declaration, so it is checked. `check_declaration` reads the requirement's own `rust,ignore` blocks and compares them with rustdoc, as follows:\n\n- **Trait impls:** it asserts equality between the requirement's impl listing (`impl Clone for Outline; impl Debug for Outline;`) and `rustdoc.trait_impls(page)`. A missing or extra trait impl fails the test.\n- **Fields and members:** it asserts equality between `link.members` and `rustdoc.member_names(page)`. This covers the `items` field and the `new` method.\n- **Signatures:** it compares `signature_parts` of the requirement's declaration with the published rustdoc declaration, and fails on any difference. This pins the struct declaration, the `items` field type `Vec<OutlineItem>`, and `pub fn new(items: Vec<OutlineItem>) -> Self`. The test `member_order_is_free_but_field_and_method_types_are_committed` shows that changed field and method types are detected.\n- **`#[non_exhaustive]`:** the attribute is part of the compared declaration text. A struct with public fields must also be non-exhaustive, which is asserted explicitly.\n\nI found no conditional or transformation obligation in this requirement that goes untested. The requirement states no behavior for `new` beyond its signature, and the `items` accessor is delegated to `requirements.sdk.outlines.items`. The reviewed test enforces each obligation the requirement states, and I found no adequacy gap.",
  "references": "34070f30c190da855a0af0db8758db88cea74ad388475c8cd2f1dfaa1fb9eb00",
